     c - multi-column output

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     cc [-ww_N] [-ll_N] [-001122]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     cc reads lines from the standard input and prints them in
     columns on the standard output, using as many columns as fit
     across the page given the width of the longest input line.

     cc recognizes the following options:

     -ww_N  Set the width of the page to _N columns (default: 80).

     -ll_N  Set the length of the page to _N lines.

     -00   Order the fields horizontally across the page.

     -11   Order the fields vertically down each column (the
          default).

     -22   A special case of -11.

     Options may also be supplied in the environment variable CC,
     separated by white space; options given on the command line
     are processed afterward and so override those taken from the
     environment.

